# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file to render the "Cite this repository"
# button, and Zenodo uses it to fill in the archive record.
#
# There is no release yet. With the first one, add `version`, `date-released`
# and the Zenodo concept DOI (`doi`), which always resolves to the latest
# archived version (plan task M.3).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cleanrules: An explainable rules engine with a Rust core"
abstract: >-
  An explainable rules engine with one Rust core and the same semantics in Rust,
  C/C++, Python, JavaScript, Java/Scala, Go and Erlang. One engine for business
  rules, expert systems (forward chaining), data validation, explaining machine
  learning models and guarding AI agents, with crisp three-valued (Kleene) and
  fuzzy logic. Every result explains which rules fired, which did not, and why.
authors:
  - family-names: "Salmeron"
    given-names: "Jose L."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7811-3716"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cleanrules/cleanrules"
url: "https://cleanrules.github.io/"
keywords:
  - rules engine
  - business rules
  - expert systems
  - data validation
  - explainable AI
  - fuzzy logic
  - three-valued logic
  - rust
